From the formula, $\omega=\frac{1}{\sqrt{L C}}$
Given, $L=8 \mathrm{H},
\begin{aligned}
& C=0.5 \mu \mathrm{ F}=0.5 \times 10^{-6} \mathrm{ F} \\
\therefore \quad & \omega=\frac{1}{\sqrt{8 \times 0.5 \times 10^{-6}}}
\end{aligned}\begin{aligned} & \Rightarrow \quad \omega=\frac{1}{2 \times 10^{-3}}=500 \\ & \Rightarrow \quad \omega=\frac{250}{\pi} \mathrm{rad} / \mathrm{s}\end{aligned}$

